# Lab 4 API tests for the VS Code REST Client extension.
# Start the API first (cd backend, npm run dev), then click "Send Request" above a test.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
# Replace with an id returned by GET or POST if ISS-101 is not in data/issues.json
@issueId = ISS-101

### T01 View all issues
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/issues

### T02 Create a valid issue
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/issues
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer unavailable",
  "description": "The shared printer is not responding.",
  "priority": "Medium"
}

### T03 Invalid create: empty title (title rule fails first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/issues
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "Missing valid title",
  "priority": "Urgent"
}

### T04 Invalid create: priority Critical is not allowed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/issues
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer unavailable",
  "description": "The shared printer is not responding.",
  "priority": "Critical"
}

### T05 Change issue status
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/issues/{{issueId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Resolved" }

### T06 Invalid status change
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/issues/{{issueId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Deleted" }

### T07 Update an unknown issue
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/issues/does-not-exist/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Resolved" }

### T08 View issues when none exist
# Replace the content of data/issues.json with [] first, then paste it back afterwards.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/issues

### T09 Create with server-owned fields (the server must ignore them)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/issues
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "HACKED-1",
  "title": "Projector flickering",
  "description": "The projector in room B204 flickers.",
  "priority": "Low",
  "status": "Resolved",
  "createdAt": "2000-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
}

### T10 Create without JSON
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/issues
Content-Type: text/plain

title=Printer

### T11 Create with malformed JSON (trailing comma)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/issues
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer unavailable",
  "description": "The shared printer is not responding.",
  "priority": "Medium",
}

### T12 Unknown route
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/fake-url
